Z||000000||pepper||10-11-2001||03:13 PM||||hi you guys<P>I'm thinking about to buy a fiero.<BR>this are my demands<BR>-V6<BR>-second edition fiero 87 or 88<BR>-much aftermarket parts available<BR>-and if its possible T-roof<P>i have to know some things<BR>what's the difference between GT en SE,<BR>what's the difference between 87 and 88<BR>what would be the best choice and why<P>I saw a picture named 49048088_012178_339x203.jpg<BR>the whit one with the diablo nose<BR>in the case mods<BR>what kind of fiero is that?<BR>can someone give me a website for more pix of that car? <P>please help me !<P>bryce<P><BR> <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||10-11-2001||03:30 PM||||87 vs. 88:  87 has the same suspension as the 84-87's.  The 88's have a redesigned suspension with bigger brakes and is much better, but parts are scarce and expensive.  If you're going to heavily mod the suspension, starting with an 87 isn't a problem, but you'll definately want to upgrade the brakes.<P>GT vs. SE:  GT is a fastback, SE is a notchback.  The GT has a V6 standard, I believe it was optional in the SE.  <P>88GT's are the most expensive, so if you want to mod a car, you can start much cheaper by getting an 87.  Get either the GT or the SE, whichever you prefer the looks of.  The 87 SE V6 would be the cheapest option (unless you go with a 4 banger)||||reg||1
